  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(252.222pt, 103.92pt, " on roughened substrates using the 3ω method, while ")
  #line-at(90pt, 124.56pt, "our Si-water conductance is significantly higher than that measured by Yu and ")
  #line-at(90pt, 145.44pt, "Nagayama ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.92pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(143.827pt, 141.36pt, "34")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(151.827pt, 145.44pt, " on microstructured surfaces with the ASTM D5470 method, underscoring ")
  #line-at(90pt, 166.08pt, "the influence of interface quality.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.92pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(249.885pt, 162pt, "44")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(257.885pt, 166.08pt, " For Al-silicone oil and PMMA-silicone oil, we did ")
  #line-at(90pt, 186.72pt, "not find prior experimental or MD benchmarks for these specific pairs; accordingly, ")
  #line-at(90pt, 207.36pt, "our measurements provide reference values for metal and polymer interfaces with van ")
  #line-at(90pt, 228.24pt, "der Waals liquids. ")
  #line-at(102pt, 248.88pt, "Comparisons with analytical models [Fig. 3(b)] and molecular dynamics simulations ")
  #line-at(90pt, 269.52pt, "show that conventional AMM and DMM generally overpredict ITC, likely because ")
  #line-at(90pt, 290.16pt, "these models are based on purely particle-like assumptions and neglect coherent effects, ")
  #line-at(90pt, 311.04pt, "which can lead to systematic deviations.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.92pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(288.768pt, 306.96pt, "45")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(296.768pt, 311.04pt, " In contrast, wettability-modified models")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.92pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(497.45pt, 306.96pt, "46")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(90pt, 331.68pt, "capture the observed trend Al-water > glass-water > Si-water (see Supplementary Sec. ")
  #line-at(90pt, 352.32pt, "S6 for details of AMM and DMM). Molecular dynamics simulations")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.92pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(413.56pt, 348.24pt, "35-37")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(432.224pt, 352.32pt, " further support ")
  #line-at(90pt, 372.96pt, "these results, particularly for hydrophilic Si-water interfaces. ")
  #line-at(102pt, 393.84pt, "Beyond comparisons with analytical models and molecular dynamics, the relative ")
  #line-at(90pt, 414.48pt, "magnitudes of the measured ITCs can also be rationalized by considering the ")
  #line-at(90pt, 435.12pt, "vibrational spectrum overlap between the solid and liquid constituents. As shown in Fig. ")
  #line-at(90pt, 455.76pt, "3(c), the vibrational density of states (VDOS) of the materials studied in this work (from ")
  #line-at(90pt, 476.64pt, "Refs. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.92pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(118.325pt, 472.56pt, "38-43")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(136.989pt, 476.64pt, ") exhibit distinct spectral characteristics that govern the degree of interfacial ")
  #line-at(90pt, 497.28pt, "coupling. Water has an exceptionally broad spectrum, spanning from sub-terahertz ")
  #line-at(90pt, 517.92pt, "collective and relaxational modes to the bending (~49 THz) and O–H stretching bands ")
  #line-at(90pt, 538.56pt, "(90-110 THz), which overlap strongly with the abundant low-frequency acoustic ")
  #line-at(90pt, 559.44pt, "phonons of Al, yielding the highest ITC for the Al-water interface. Glass exhibits a ")
  #line-at(90pt, 580.08pt, "wide phonon spectrum with a cutoff around ~20 THz and a characteristic boson peak ")
  #line-at(90pt, 600.72pt, "in the terahertz range, enabling partial overlap with water’s low-frequency modes and ")
  #line-at(90pt, 621.36pt, "resulting in the next-highest ITC. In contrast, crystalline Si shows a main VDOS peak ")
  #line-at(90pt, 642.24pt, "near 14 THz but has comparatively weak low-frequency states, and the additional ")
  #line-at(90pt, 662.88pt, "presence of a native oxide and hydration layer further suppresses vibrational coupling, ")
  #line-at(90pt, 683.52pt, "leading to a lower Si-water ITC. Silicone oil exhibits dominant vibrational bands in the ")
  #line-at(90pt, 704.16pt, "mid-infrared (~22 THz), but also possesses low-frequency relaxational modes that can ")
  #line-at(90pt, 725.04pt, "couple with Al’s acoustic phonons; consequently, the Al-silicone oil ITC is comparable ")
  #line-at(90pt, 745.68pt, "to that of glass-water. Finally, the PMMA-silicone oil interface yields the lowest ITC, ")
  #line-at(90pt, 766.32pt, "since the primary VDOS peak of PMMA lies at ~1.7 THz and is largely offset from the ")
]

